Handle LiteLLM 1.91.1 PermissionDeniedError as a non-retryable provider failure.
Aider enumerates LiteLLM exceptions strictly, so the new class otherwise
prevents every completion, including requests to Ollama.

--- a/aider/exceptions.py
+++ b/aider/exceptions.py
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@
     ExInfo("JSONSchemaValidationError", True, None),
     ExInfo("NotFoundError", False, None),
     ExInfo("OpenAIError", True, None),
+    ExInfo("PermissionDeniedError", False, "The API provider denied permission for this request."),
     ExInfo(
         "RateLimitError",
         True,
